        <param name="permission">the permission to check against.</param>
        <summary>
        </summary>
        <returns>true if the specified permission is implied by this object, false if not.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Checks if the specified permission's actions are "implied by" this object's actions. This must be implemented by subclasses of Permission, as they are the only ones that can impose semantics on a Permission object. The implies method is used by the AccessController to determine whether a requested permission is implied by another permission that is known to be valid in the current execution context.</para>
